Whitecube Trainer standalone package
===================================

The upstream NOTICE covers the full Whitecube repository. This standalone
package contains Trainer, its pipeline, the GTK theme and trainer icon only.
It does not bundle the compositor, Electron, wlroots, cairo or other apps.

Launch Whitecube Trainer from your applications menu or run:

    whitecube-trainer
    whitecube-trainer-cli --help
    whitecube-trainer-cli --doctor

The standalone commands deliberately differ from cube-train and whitecube-train
provided by whitecube-desktop, so the packages can coexist without overwriting
one another. No Whitecube compositor or desktop session is required. GTK uses
your current Wayland or X11 desktop and honors GDK_BACKEND when explicitly set.

Training runtime
----------------
The desktop never imports PyTorch. Select a Python interpreter in Train, then
use Check runtime. The recommended python3-torch and python3-numpy packages
provide a system CPU runtime. Existing CUDA virtual environments can be selected
instead. PyArrow is optional for Parquet, safetensors for weights export and
Jupyter/ipykernel for notebook execution. Nothing is downloaded by package
maintainer scripts; this package has no maintainer scripts.

GTK >= 4.12 and libadwaita >= 1.5 are required. Older distributions must upgrade
these libraries before this package can be installed.

User data
---------
Runs default to ~/train-out (override WHITECUBE_TRAIN_OUT). Preferences are in
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/whitecube/trainer.json, with ~/.config as the default.
Jobs use $XDG_STATE_HOME/whitecube/trainer, with ~/.local/state as the default.
Removing the package preserves runs, environments and settings.

Rebuilding
----------
From apps/cube-train:

    ./packaging/build-deb.sh

Output goes to dist/whitecube-trainer_<version>_all.deb with a SHA256 sidecar.
--output-dir, --version and --epoch are supported. SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH or the
repository's latest commit timestamp makes identical source builds reproducible.
The build requires Python 3, git, dpkg and dpkg-deb; it performs no installation,
network access, compilation or privileged actions.
